{
  "$schema": "../signalset.schema.json",
  "vehicle": "Ford-F-150-Lightning-2022",
  "description": "Ford F-150 Lightning, 2022-2025. Community data from OBDb, selected for battery diagnostics: HV battery (BECM 7E4), charger (SOBDM 7E2), drive unit (7E6), DC/DC (746), 12 V battery monitor (726). 11-bit CAN, standard ISO-TP, UDS 0x22 reads only. NOT read on a vehicle by this project.",
  "provenance": {
    "derivedFrom": "OBDb/Ford-F-150-Lightning @ bb26b0f293 (2026-11-13), signalsets/v3/default.json (CC BY-SA 4.0)",
    "confidence": "Imported from OBDb by tools/obdb-import (map: tools/obdb-import/ford-f150-lightning.map.json). The bit layouts and scaling are OBDb's, unchanged; test/obdb_import_test.dart replays OBDb's captured replies from 2022-2025 trucks and gets OBDb's expected values. This project has not read a Lightning. Open before relying on it: the sign of HVBAT_CURRENT (the app expects positive = discharge; check against a known charge and a known load), what 485C 'battery capacity' means (rated or present), and whether a cheap ELM327 clone handles the commands OBDb marks fcm1.",
    "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0"
  },
  "protocol": {
    "canFormat": "11bit",
    "obdProtocol": 6,
    "note": "ISO 15765-4 CAN 11-bit/500k. Each module has its own request id and answers on id+8 (BECM 7E4 -> 7EC). OBDb marks some commands fcm1 (flow-control mode 1); the field is kept but this app does not act on it yet."
  },
